{"id":"mahabharata-7-087","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":87,"title":"सप्ताशीतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 87 · Satyaki sets out","summary":{"en":"Satyaki agrees, bows to the king and promises to cut a path through Drona's host to reach Arjuna. He sets out with his chariot while the Pandavas bless him and the Panchalas follow.","kn":"ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿ ಒಪ್ಪಿ ರಾಜನಿಗೆ ನಮಿಸಿ ದ್ರೋಣನ ಸೈನ್ಯವನ್ನು ಸೀಳಿ ಅರ್ಜುನನನ್ನು ತಲುಪುವೆನೆಂದು ಪ್ರತಿಜ್ಞೆ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಪಾಂಡವರ ಆಶೀರ್ವಾದದೊಂದಿಗೆ, ಪಾಂಚಾಲರು ಹಿಂಬಾಲಿಸುತ್ತಿರಲು ಹೊರಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"सात्यकि मान जाता है, राजा को प्रणाम कर द्रोण की सेना चीरकर अर्जुन तक पहुँचने का वचन देता है। पाण्डवों के आशीर्वाद और पाञ्चालों के अनुसरण के साथ वह रथ पर निकलता है।","te":"సాత్యకి అంగీకరించి రాజుకు నమస్కరించి ద్రోణుని సేనను చీల్చి అర్జునుని చేరతానని మాటిస్తాడు. పాండవుల ఆశీస్సులతో, పాంచాలులు వెంట రాగా రథంపై బయలుదేరతాడు.","ta":"சாத்யகி ஒப்புக்கொண்டு மன்னரை வணங்கி த்ரோணரின் படையைப் பிளந்து அர்ஜுனனை அடைவதாக உறுதியளிக்கிறான். பாண்டவரின் ஆசியுடனும் பாஞ்சாலர் பின்தொடரவும் தேரில் புறப்படுகிறான்.","ml":"സാത്യകി സമ്മതിച്ച് രാജാവിനെ വണങ്ങുന്നു; ദ്രോണരുടെ സേനയിലൂടെ വഴിവെട്ടി അർജുനന്റെ അടുത്തെത്തുമെന്ന് വാഗ്ദാനം ചെയ്യുന്നു. പാണ്ഡവർ അനുഗ്രഹിക്കുമ്പോൾ പാഞ്ചാലർ പിന്തുടരുന്ന തേരിൽ അദ്ദേഹം പുറപ്പെടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.87; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जयद्रथवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jayadrathavadha Parva (Slaying of Jayadratha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"धर्मराजस्य तद्वाक्यं निशम्य शिनिपुंगवः ।\nपार्थाच्च भयमाशङ्कन्परित्यागान्महीपतेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the Dharma king's words, the bull of the Shinis feared Partha's displeasure if he abandoned the king."}},{"n":2,"text":"अपवादं ह्यात्मनश्च लोकाद्रक्षन्विशेषतः ।\nन मां भीत इति ब्रूयुरायान्तं फल्गुनं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Above all he wished to guard himself from the world's reproach, so that none could say, \"He was afraid, as he approached Phalguna.\""}},{"n":3,"text":"निश्चित्य बहुधैवं स सात्यकिर्युद्धदुर्मदः ।\nधर्मराजमिदं वाक्यमब्रवीत्पुरुषर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having weighed this in many ways, Satyaki, reckless in battle, that best of men, spoke these words to the Dharma king."}},{"n":4,"text":"कृतां चेन्मन्यसे रक्षां स्वस्ति तेऽस्तु विशां पते ।\nअनुयास्यामि बीभत्सुं करिष्ये वचनं तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If you think your protection is assured, then good fortune be with you, lord of the people; I will follow Bibhatsu and do as you say."}},{"n":5,"text":"न हि मे पाण्डवात्कश्चित्त्रिषु लोकेषु विद्यते ।\nयो वै प्रियतरो राजन्सत्यमेतद्ब्रवीमि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the three worlds, O king, there is no Pandava dearer to me than he; I tell you this truly."}},{"n":6,"text":"तस्याहं पदवीं यास्ये संदेशात्तव मानद ।\nत्वत्कृते न च मे किंचिदकर्तव्यं कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"At your command, giver of honor, I will follow his path; for your sake there is nothing I will not do."}},{"n":7,"text":"यथा हि मे गुरोर्वाक्यं विशिष्टं द्विपदां वर ।\nतथा तवापि वचनं विशिष्टतरमेव मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"As my teacher's word is weighty to me, best of men, so yours is weightier still."}},{"n":8,"text":"प्रिये हि तव वर्तेते भ्रातरौ कृष्णपाण्डवौ ।\nतयोः प्रिये स्थितं चैव विद्धि मां राजपुंगव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Both brothers, Krishna and the Pandava, delight in what pleases you; know me, bull among kings, to be devoted to what pleases them."}},{"n":9,"text":"तवाज्ञां शिरसा गृह्य पाण्डवार्थमहं प्रभो ।\nभित्त्वेदं दुर्भिदं सैन्यं प्रयास्ये नरसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking your command on my head, lord, I shall go for the Pandavas' sake, breaking through this hard-to-break army, best of men."}},{"n":10,"text":"द्रोणानीकं विशाम्येष क्रुद्धो झष इवार्णवम् ।\nतत्र यास्यामि यत्रासौ राजन्राजा जयद्रथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I enter Drona's host, enraged, as a fish enters the sea, and go where King Jayadratha is, O king,"}},{"n":11,"text":"यत्र सेनां समाश्रित्य भीतस्तिष्ठति पाण्डवात् ।\nगुप्तो रथवरश्रेष्ठैर्द्रौणिकर्णकृपादिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where he stands in the shelter of his army, afraid of the Pandava, guarded by the best of chariot-warriors, Drona's son, Karna, Kripa and others."}},{"n":12,"text":"इतस्त्रियोजनं मन्ये तमध्वानं विशां पते ।\nयत्र तिष्ठति पार्थोऽसौ जयद्रथवधोद्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think that place is three yojanas from here, lord of the people, where Partha stands intent on killing Jayadratha."}},{"n":13,"text":"त्रियोजनगतस्यापि तस्य यास्याम्यहं पदम् ।\nआसैन्धववधाद्राजन्सुदृढेनान्तरात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even if he had gone three yojanas, I would follow his track with a firm heart, until Saindhava is killed."}},{"n":14,"text":"अनादिष्टस्तु गुरुणा को नु युध्येत मानवः ।\nआदिष्टस्तु त्वया राजन्को न युध्येत मादृशः ।\nअभिजानामि तं देशं यत्र यास्याम्यहं प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"What man would fight without his teacher's order? But ordered by you, O king, who like me would not fight? I know the region to which I shall go, lord."}},{"n":15,"text":"हुडशक्तिगदाप्रासखड्गचर्मर्ष्टितोमरम् ।\nइष्वस्त्रवरसंबाधं क्षोभयिष्ये बलार्णवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall churn up that ocean of an army, crowded with hudas, spears, maces, lances, swords, shields, rishtis, tomaras, and the best bows and weapons."}},{"n":16,"text":"यदेतत्कुञ्जरानीकं साहस्रमनुपश्यसि ।\nकुलमञ्जनकं नाम यत्रैते वीर्यशालिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This thousand-strong elephant force that you see, called Kulamanjanaka, where these mighty ones are,"}},{"n":17,"text":"आस्थिता बहुभिर्म्लेच्छैर्युद्धशौण्डैः प्रहारिभिः ।\nनागा मेघनिभा राजन्क्षरन्त इव तोयदाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Is manned by many mlecchas, expert in battle and good at striking, elephants like clouds, O king, dripping like rain-clouds."}},{"n":18,"text":"नैते जातु निवर्तेरन्प्रेषिता हस्तिसादिभिः ।\nअन्यत्र हि वधादेषां नास्ति राजन्पराजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sent forward by their mahouts, they would never turn back; for them, O king, there is no defeat except by death."}},{"n":19,"text":"अथ यान्रथिनो राजन्समन्तादनुपश्यसि ।\nएते रुक्मरथा नाम राजपुत्रा महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the chariot-fighters you see all around, O king, are princes called the Rukmarathas, great chariot-warriors,"}},{"n":20,"text":"रथेष्वस्त्रेषु निपुणा नागेषु च विशां पते ।\nधनुर्वेदे गताः पारं मुष्टियुद्धे च कोविदाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Skilled in chariots, weapons and elephants, lord of men, masters of the science of the bow, and expert in fist-fighting,"}},{"n":21,"text":"गदायुद्धविशेषज्ञा नियुद्धकुशलास्तथा ।\nखड्गप्रहरणे युक्ताः संपाते चासिचर्मणोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Skilled in mace fighting and wrestling, practiced in striking with the sword and in the clash of sword and shield."}},{"n":22,"text":"शूराश्च कृतविद्याश्च स्पर्धन्ते च परस्परम् ।\nनित्यं च समरे राजन्विजिगीषन्ति मानवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They are brave and learned, vie with one another, and always long to conquer men in battle."}},{"n":23,"text":"कर्णेन विजिता राजन्दुःशासनमनुव्रताः ।\nएतांस्तु वासुदेवोऽपि रथोदारान्प्रशंसति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Conquered by Karna, O king, they are devoted to Duhshasana. Even Vasudeva praises these noble chariot-fighters."}},{"n":24,"text":"सततं प्रियकामाश्च कर्णस्यैते वशे स्थिताः ।\nतस्यैव वचनाद्राजन्निवृत्ताः श्वेतवाहनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They always wish to please Karna and live under his sway; at his word, O king, they turned back from the white-horsed Arjuna."}},{"n":25,"text":"ते न क्षता न च श्रान्ता दृढावरणकार्मुकाः ।\nमदर्थं विष्ठिता नूनं धार्तराष्ट्रस्य शासनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Unwounded and untired, with strong armor and bows, they stand there to face me, surely, on Dhritarashtra's son's order."}},{"n":26,"text":"एतान्प्रमथ्य संग्रामे प्रियार्थं तव कौरव ।\nप्रयास्यामि ततः पश्चात्पदवीं सव्यसाचिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having crushed them in battle for your pleasure, Kaurava, I shall afterward follow the track of Savyasachin."}},{"n":27,"text":"यांस्त्वेतानपरान्राजन्नागान्सप्तशतानि च ।\nप्रेक्षसे वर्मसंछन्नान्किरातैः समधिष्ठितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And those other elephants, seven hundred, that you see covered in armor and ridden by Kiratas,"}},{"n":28,"text":"किरातराजो यान्प्रादाद्गृहीतः सव्यसाचिना ।\nस्वलंकृतांस्तथा प्रेष्यानिच्छञ्जीवितमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That the Kirata king gave when he was captured by Savyasachin, richly adorned, as servants, wishing to save his own life,"}},{"n":29,"text":"आसन्नेते पुरा राजंस्तव कर्मकरा दृढम् ।\nत्वामेवाद्य युयुत्सन्ते पश्य कालस्य पर्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They were once firm servants of yours, O king; now they wish to fight you. See how time turns."}},{"n":30,"text":"तेषामेते महामात्राः किराता युद्धदुर्मदाः ।\nहस्तिशिक्षाविदश्चैव सर्वे चैवाग्नियोनयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their chief men, the Kiratas, reckless in battle, and all of them skilled in training elephants and born of fire,"}},{"n":31,"text":"एते विनिर्जिताः सर्वे संग्रामे सव्यसाचिना ।\nमदर्थमद्य संयत्ता दुर्योधनवशानुगाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All these were defeated in battle by Savyasachin, and today they are ready against me, under Duryodhana's sway."}},{"n":32,"text":"एतान्भित्त्वा शरै राजन्किरातान्युद्धदुर्मदान् ।\nसैन्धवस्य वधे युक्तमनुयास्यामि पाण्डवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having broken these Kiratas, reckless in battle, with arrows, O king, I shall follow the Pandava, who is engaged in killing Saindhava."}},{"n":33,"text":"ये त्वेते सुमहानागा अञ्जनस्य कुलोद्भवाः ।\nकर्कशाश्च विनीताश्च प्रभिन्नकरटामुखाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And those huge elephants, born of the Anjana line, rough and well trained, with temples broken by rut,"}},{"n":34,"text":"जाम्बूनदमयैः सर्वैर्वर्मभिः सुविभूषिताः ।\nलब्धलक्ष्या रणे राजन्नैरावणसमा युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"All finely adorned with golden armor, accurate in aim, in battle like Airavata, O king,"}},{"n":35,"text":"उत्तरात्पर्वतादेते तीक्ष्णैर्दस्युभिरास्थिताः ।\nकर्कशैः प्रवरैर्योधैः कार्ष्णायसतनुच्छदैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Are ridden by fierce dasyus from the northern mountain, hard, excellent warriors clad in black iron armor."}},{"n":36,"text":"सन्ति गोयोनयश्चात्र सन्ति वानरयोनयः ।\nअनेकयोनयश्चान्ये तथा मानुषयोनयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among them are some born of cows, some born of monkeys, some of many kinds, and some born of men."}},{"n":37,"text":"अनीकमसतामेतद्धूमवर्णमुदीर्यते ।\nम्लेच्छानां पापकर्तॄणां हिमवद्दुर्गवासिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This smoke-colored host belongs to the wicked mlecchas, doers of sinful deeds, who live in the strongholds of the Himalaya."}},{"n":38,"text":"एतद्दुर्योधनो लब्ध्वा समग्रं नागमण्डलम् ।\nकृपं च सौमदत्तिं च द्रोणं च रथिनां वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having obtained this whole circle of elephants, and Kripa, Somadatta's son, and Drona, best of charioteers,"}},{"n":39,"text":"सिन्धुराजं तथा कर्णमवमन्यत पाण्डवान् ।\nकृतार्थमथ चात्मानं मन्यते कालचोदितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the Sindhu king and Karna, Duryodhana, driven by time, scorned the Pandavas and thinks himself successful."}},{"n":40,"text":"ते च सर्वेऽनुसंप्राप्ता मम नाराचगोचरम् ।\nन विमोक्ष्यन्ति कौन्तेय यद्यपि स्युर्मनोजवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All of them, now come within the range of my iron arrows, son of Kunti, will not escape, even if swift as thought."}},{"n":41,"text":"तेन संभाविता नित्यं परवीर्योपजीविना ।\nविनाशमुपयास्यन्ति मच्छरौघनिपीडिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Always esteemed by him, living off others' strength, they will go to destruction, crushed by floods of my arrows."}},{"n":42,"text":"ये त्वेते रथिनो राजन्दृश्यन्ते काञ्चनध्वजाः ।\nएते दुर्वारणा नाम काम्बोजा यदि ते श्रुताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And those chariot-fighters, O king, with golden banners that you see, are the Kambojas called Durvaranas, if you have heard of them."}},{"n":43,"text":"शूराश्च कृतविद्याश्च धनुर्वेदे च निष्ठिताः ।\nसंहताश्च भृशं ह्येते अन्योन्यस्य हितैषिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They are brave, learned, perfected in archery, tightly united, each wishing the other's good."}},{"n":44,"text":"अक्षौहिण्यश्च संरब्धा धार्तराष्ट्रस्य भारत ।\nयत्ता मदर्थं तिष्ठन्ति कुरुवीराभिरक्षिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the Dhartarashtra's enraged akshauhinis, guarded by Kuru heroes, stand ready for me."}},{"n":45,"text":"अप्रमत्ता महाराज मामेव प्रत्युपस्थिताः ।\nतांस्त्वहं प्रमथिष्यामि तृणानीव हुताशनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Alert, great king, they have come to face me alone; I shall crush them as fire crushes straw."}},{"n":46,"text":"तस्मात्सर्वानुपासङ्गान्सर्वोपकरणानि च ।\nरथे कुर्वन्तु मे राजन्यथावद्रथकल्पकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore let the chariot-fitters put on my chariot, O king, all the quivers and equipment as is proper."}},{"n":47,"text":"अस्मिंस्तु खलु संग्रामे ग्राह्यं विविधमायुधम् ।\nयथोपदिष्टमाचार्यैः कार्यः पञ्चगुणो रथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this battle, various weapons must be taken; as the teachers taught, the chariot must have five sets of gear."}},{"n":48,"text":"काम्बोजैर्हि समेष्यामि क्रुद्धैराशीविषोपमैः ।\nनानाशस्त्रसमावापैर्विविधायुधयोधिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall meet the Kambojas, enraged like venomous snakes, fighting with many weapons and with a variety of arms."}},{"n":49,"text":"किरातैश्च समेष्यामि विषकल्पैः प्रहारिभिः ।\nलालितैः सततं राज्ञा दुर्योधनहितैषिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall meet the Kiratas, who strike like poison, long indulged by the king, wishing Duryodhana's good."}},{"n":50,"text":"शकैश्चापि समेष्यामि शक्रतुल्यपराक्रमैः ।\nअग्निकल्पैर्दुराधर्षैः प्रदीप्तैरिव पावकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall meet the Shakas too, equal in valor to Indra, fiery, hard to withstand, like blazing flames."}},{"n":51,"text":"तथान्यैर्विविधैर्योधैः कालकल्पैर्दुरासदैः ।\nसमेष्यामि रणे राजन्बहुभिर्युद्धदुर्मदैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And I shall meet in battle, O king, many other warriors, hard to approach and like death itself, reckless in the fight."}},{"n":52,"text":"तस्माद्वै वाजिनो मुख्या विश्रान्ताः शुभलक्षणाः ।\nउपावृत्ताश्च पीताश्च पुनर्युज्यन्तु मे रथे ॥","meaning":{"en":"So let my best horses, rested and of fine marks, be turned back, watered, and yoked again to my chariot.\""}},{"n":53,"text":"तस्य सर्वानुपासङ्गान्सर्वोपकरणानि च ।\nरथे प्रास्थापयद्राजा शस्त्राणि विविधानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king had all his quivers and equipment and various weapons placed on his chariot."}},{"n":54,"text":"ततस्तान्सर्वतो मुक्त्वा सदश्वांश्चतुरो जनाः ।\nरसवत्पाययामासुः पानं मदसमीरिणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the men unyoked the four fine horses all around and gave them a flavorful drink that stirs spirit."}},{"n":55,"text":"पीतोपवृत्तान्स्नातांश्च जग्धान्नान्समलंकृतान् ।\nविनीतशल्यांस्तुरगांश्चतुरो हेममालिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The four horses, watered, rolled, bathed, fed, adorned, free of arrows, wearing golden garlands,"}},{"n":56,"text":"तान्यत्तान्रुक्मवर्णाभान्विनीताञ्शीघ्रगामिनः ।\nसंहृष्टमनसोऽव्यग्रान्विधिवत्कल्पिते रथे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Golden in color, well trained, swift, glad at heart and calm, they yoked to the chariot, made ready as the rules direct,"}},{"n":57,"text":"महाध्वजेन सिंहेन हेमकेसरमालिना ।\nसंवृते केतनैर्हेमैर्मणिविद्रुमचित्रितैः ।\nपाण्डुराभ्रप्रकाशाभिः पताकाभिरलंकृते ॥","meaning":{"en":"A chariot with a great lion banner with a golden mane and garland, covered with golden standards decked with jewels and coral, adorned with pennants shining like white clouds,"}},{"n":58,"text":"हेमदण्डोच्छ्रितच्छत्रे बहुशस्त्रपरिच्छदे ।\nयोजयामास विधिवद्धेमभाण्डविभूषितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With a parasol raised on a golden pole, and many weapons in it, the horses decked with golden ornaments."}},{"n":59,"text":"दारुकस्यानुजो भ्राता सूतस्तस्य प्रियः सखा ।\nन्यवेदयद्रथं युक्तं वासवस्येव मातलिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Daruka's younger brother, his dear friend, the charioteer, reported the chariot ready, as Matali does for Vasava."}},{"n":60,"text":"ततः स्नातः शुचिर्भूत्वा कृतकौतुकमङ्गलः ।\nस्नातकानां सहस्रस्य स्वर्णनिष्कानदापयत् ।\nआशीर्वादैः परिष्वक्तः सात्यकिः श्रीमतां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Satyaki, best of the prosperous, having bathed and purified himself and performed auspicious rites, had golden nishkas given to a thousand snatakas, embraced by their blessings."}},{"n":61,"text":"ततः स मधुपर्कार्हः पीत्वा कैलावतं मधु ।\nलोहिताक्षो बभौ तत्र मदविह्वललोचनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he, worthy of the honey-offering, drank Kailavata honey, and with his reddened eyes rolling with the drink, he shone."}},{"n":62,"text":"आलभ्य वीरकांस्यं च हर्षेण महतान्वितः ।\nद्विगुणीकृततेजा हि प्रज्वलन्निव पावकः ।\nउत्सङ्गे धनुरादाय सशरं रथिनां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Touching the hero's bronze, filled with great joy, his splendor doubled, blazing as it were like fire, that best of charioteers took up his bow and arrows on his lap."}},{"n":63,"text":"कृतस्वस्त्ययनो विप्रैः कवची समलंकृतः ।\nलाजैर्गन्धैस्तथा माल्यैः कन्याभिश्चाभिनन्दितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having had blessings spoken by brahmins, armored and adorned, greeted with parched grain, perfumes, garlands and maidens,"}},{"n":64,"text":"युधिष्ठिरस्य चरणावभिवाद्य कृताञ्जलिः ।\nतेन मूर्धन्युपाघ्रात आरुरोह महारथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He bowed to Yudhishthira's feet with joined palms, was kissed on the head by him, and mounted the great chariot."}},{"n":65,"text":"ततस्ते वाजिनो हृष्टाः सुपुष्टा वातरंहसः ।\nअजय्या जैत्रमूहुस्तं विकुर्वन्तः स्म सैन्धवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then those glad, sturdy horses, swift as the wind, unconquerable, Saindhava horses, bore him to victory, prancing."}},{"n":66,"text":"अथ हर्षपरीताङ्गः सात्यकिर्भीममब्रवीत् ।\nत्वं भीम रक्ष राजानमेतत्कार्यतमं हि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Satyaki, his body full of joy, said to Bhima: \"Bhima, guard the king; that is your chief task."}},{"n":67,"text":"अहं भित्त्वा प्रवेक्ष्यामि कालपक्वमिदं बलम् ।\nआयत्यां च तदात्वे च श्रेयो राज्ञोऽभिरक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall break in and enter this army, ripe for death. For the future and for the present, guarding the king is best."}},{"n":68,"text":"जानीषे मम वीर्यं त्वं तव चाहमरिंदम ।\nतस्माद्भीम निवर्तस्व मम चेदिच्छसि प्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You know my strength, and I know yours, tamer of foes. So turn back, Bhima, if you wish to please me.\""}},{"n":69,"text":"तथोक्तः सात्यकिं प्राह व्रज त्वं कार्यसिद्धये ।\nअहं राज्ञः करिष्यामि रक्षां पुरुषसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"So addressed, Bhima said to Satyaki, \"Go, accomplish your task. I shall guard the king, best of men.\""}},{"n":70,"text":"एवमुक्तः प्रत्युवाच भीमसेनं स माधवः ।\nगच्छ गच्छ द्रुतं पार्थ ध्रुवोऽद्य विजयो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Told so, Madhava replied to Bhimasena: \"Go, go quickly, Partha; my victory is certain today."}},{"n":71,"text":"यन्मे स्निग्धोऽनुरक्तश्च त्वमद्य वशगः स्थितः ।\nनिमित्तानि च धन्यानि यथा भीम वदन्ति मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because you, loving and devoted to me, stand under my sway, and because the omens, Bhima, speak well to me,"}},{"n":72,"text":"निहते सैन्धवे पापे पाण्डवेन महात्मना ।\nपरिष्वजिष्ये राजानं धर्मात्मानं न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the wicked Saindhava has been killed by the great-souled Pandava, I shall embrace the righteous king, without doubt.\""}},{"n":73,"text":"एतावदुक्त्वा भीमं तु विसृज्य च महामनाः ।\nसंप्रैक्षत्तावकं सैन्यं व्याघ्रो मृगगणानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this to Bhima and dismissed him, the high-minded one looked at your army as a tiger looks at herds of deer."}},{"n":74,"text":"तं दृष्ट्वा प्रविविक्षन्तं सैन्यं तव जनाधिप ।\nभूय एवाभवन्मूढं सुभृशं चाप्यकम्पत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him about to enter, lord of the people, your army again grew confused and shook greatly."}},{"n":75,"text":"ततः प्रयातः सहसा सैन्यं तव स सात्यकिः ।\nदिदृक्षुरर्जुनं राजन्धर्मराजस्य शासनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Satyaki suddenly went forth against your army, eager to see Arjuna, at the Dharma king's command."}}]}]}